cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the paper (preferred-citation); if you use the blp-research code, also cite the software."
title: "blp-research: text-based regional indicators from Business Liaison Program notes and a grounded report-drafting assistant"
abstract: >-
  Companion code for a four-study research program on the Bank of Thailand's
  Business Liaison Program: anonymization and coding of Thai-language interview
  notes, sector-weighted and composition-adjusted diffusion indices,
  pseudo-real-time nowcasting with Clark-West and Diebold-Mariano tests, a
  retrieval-augmented drafting assistant with a number and citation verifier,
  and the design and power analysis of a randomized crossover experiment.
  Runs end to end on synthetic data.
type: software
authors:
